@startuml auth-refresh-flow
' Refresh token lifecycle (ADR-008): sign-up -> login -> silent refresh -> sign-out.
' Front = Vue SPA (Pinia store, access token in memory only).
' API   = Rust/Axum backend. Refresh tokens: opaque, single use, stored SHA-256 hashed.

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

actor User
box "Browser"
  participant "Vue SPA\n(Pinia auth store)" as Front
end box
box "Backend"
  participant "Rust API\n(Axum)" as API
  database "PostgreSQL\n(users, refresh_tokens)" as DB
end box

== Sign-up ==
User -> Front : email + password
Front -> API : POST /api/auth/register\n{email, password}
API -> DB : INSERT user (argon2id password hash)
API --> Front : 201 {id, email}

== Login ==
User -> Front : email + password
Front -> API : POST /api/auth/login\n{email, password}
API -> DB : SELECT user by email\n+ argon2id verify
API -> API : issue JWT access token (15 min)\nissue opaque refresh token (~244 bits)
API -> DB : INSERT refresh token\n(SHA-256 hash only, expires in 30 d)
API --> Front : 200 {access_token}\nSet-Cookie: refresh_token=...\nHttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict;\nPath=/api/auth; Max-Age=30d
note right of Front
  access_token kept **in memory** (Pinia),
  never in localStorage.
  refresh_token: HttpOnly cookie —
  invisible to JavaScript.
end note

== Authenticated usage ==
User -> Front : launches a search
Front -> API : POST /api/searches\nAuthorization: Bearer <access_token>
API --> Front : 202 {job_id}

... ~15 min later, the access token has expired ...

Front -> API : GET /api/searches\nAuthorization: Bearer <expired token>
API --> Front : 401 invalid or missing access token

group withAuth: refresh once, then retry
  Front -> API : POST /api/auth/refresh\nCookie: refresh_token (sent automatically)
  API -> DB : SELECT by SHA-256(presented)
  API -> DB : DELETE consumed token  «single use»
  API -> API : check expiry\nissue new access + refresh pair
  API -> DB : INSERT new token hash
  API --> Front : 200 {access_token}\nSet-Cookie: refresh_token=<new>  «rotation»
  Front -> API : GET /api/searches\nAuthorization: Bearer <new access_token>
  API --> Front : 200 [...]
end

group Replay of a consumed/stolen refresh token
  Front -> API : POST /api/auth/refresh\nCookie: refresh_token=<already consumed>
  API -> DB : SELECT by hash -> not found
  API --> Front : 401 + Set-Cookie cleared (Max-Age=0)
  Front -> Front : clear in-memory token
  Front -> User : redirect to /login
end

== Page reload (silent session restore) ==
User -> Front : F5 — in-memory access token is lost
Front -> Front : router guard: not authenticated\n-> tryRefresh()
Front -> API : POST /api/auth/refresh\nCookie: refresh_token (survived the reload)
API -> DB : rotate (consume + insert new)
API --> Front : 200 {access_token} + new cookie
Front -> User : session restored, no login prompt

== Sign-out ==
User -> Front : clicks logout
Front -> Front : clear in-memory access token
Front -> API : POST /api/auth/logout\nCookie: refresh_token
API -> DB : DELETE token (revocation, idempotent)
API --> Front : 204\nSet-Cookie: refresh_token=; Max-Age=0
Front -> User : redirect to /login

note over API, DB
  Background reaper (ADR-016) also purges
  expired refresh tokens every 60 s.
end note

@enduml
